    "guid": "695F887A7CB84317A0538FC5FD9F44D0",
    "previous_id": 867154,
    "previous_guid": "EB2E057BC96A4AA89FE1CE02C8CAEDBE",
    "section": "<p>Measuring liquid dispensing</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Depress the plunger on the micropipette to the first stop.\n\nIt is worth taking time to familiarize your self with the micropipette plunger positions if you have not used one before/recently. The first stop refers to the initial resistance of the plunger but is not fully depressed. The second stop is when the plunger is fully depressed. The up position is the default position.\n \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31557,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
